How can I dynamically update data in Flask without reloading the page? I'm trying to create something like Google Suggest Tool and I'm listening to input changes and sending data via GET method. However, when I try to print the data dynamically in HTML using Jinja, the variable doesn't update dynamically and prints an empty list. Here's the code I'm using:

For sending data using GET method:
```
$("#search_form_input").keyup(function(){
    var some_var = $(this).val();
    $.ajax({
        url: "",
        type: "get",
        data:{jsdata: some_var},
        success: function(response) {

        },
        error: function(xhr) {
            //Handle error
        }
    });
});
```

For handling data and sending it to Google API:
```
@app.route('/', methods=['GET', 'POST'])
def start_page_data():
    query_for_suggest = request.args.get('jsdata')

    if query_for_suggest == None:
        suggestions_list = ['',]
        pass
    else:
        suggestions_list = []
        r = requests.get('http://suggestqueries.google.com/complete/search?output=toolbar&hl=ru&q={}&gl=in'.format(query_for_suggest), 'lxml')
        soup = BeautifulSoup(r.content)
        suggestions = soup.find_all('suggestion')
        for suggestion in suggestions:
            suggestions_list.append(suggestion.attrs['data'])
        print(suggestions_list)
    return render_template('start_page.html', suggestions_list=suggestions_list)
```

For printing data dynamically in HTML using Jinja:
```
<label id="value_lable">
    {% for suggestion in suggestions_list %}
       {{ suggestion }}
    {% endfor %}
</label>
```
